    <time>1794932503</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 2.5.0:
  * v2.5.0
  * Publish the DB image with the workflow's own token (#5152)
  * Bump FDW version to v2.3.0 (#5151)
  * Check root's way into Steampipe's database too, and give an include line its own message
  * Do not count a samerole rule as letting root into the postgres database
  * Say an upgrade leaves pg_hba.conf behind only across major versions, and check the postgres database and include lines
  * Check the pg_hba.conf the next start uses, and give advice that holds
  * Add tests for pg_hba.conf checks and advice that are wrong
  * Say in GetClientCount's doc how it counts a service an older version started
  * Put writeFakeInstall's doc back on it and say what the fakes now change
  * Keep the db_local unit tests inside CI's 30s limit
  * Count another role's sessions by their database and user, not by an application name postgres's own processes also carry
  * Count an older version's clients with the service password, see other roles' sessions, and drop the --force advice
  * Test that a pg_hba.conf link to a missing file is followed up from a linked folder
  * Test that service stop counts an older version's clients with the service password
  * Count an older version's clients on service stop too, and follow chained pg_hba.conf links
  * Add tests for service stop on an older version's service and chained pg_hba.conf links
  * Restore pg_hba.conf links in place, count an older service's clients, and take the install port late
  * Add tests for pg_hba.conf links, the abort advice and counting an older service's clients
  * Give only the move advice when a data move stops on a too-long socket path
  * Add a test that a too-long socket path on a data move gives only the move advice
  * Stop on an unfinished or other-major data folder, closes #5137 (#5142)
  * Point the installation tests' pg_dump at the socket in the data directory
  * Say what to do when an older install's database cannot be used, refs #5111 (#5146)
  * A connection whose plugin block failed to load is reported in error, not ready (#5145)
  * A connection config change made while a plugin is starting is sent once it has started (#5144)
  * Add tests that guard the data-folder and pg_hba fixes (#5143)
  * Keep data reachable when the socket path is too long, and keep pg_hba.conf links
  * Add tests for socket path advice, link restore and older-version shutdown
  * Keep a leftover backup out of the kept database closes #5136 (#5139)
  * Stop at once, naming the role, when postgres says root does not exist
  * Format the socket test
  * Tell the user what to do for every pg_hba.conf stop, and stop a restart that would fail
  * Make an install directory with a comma or a double quote work
  * service status --all no longer panics on an exited process closes #5133 (#5140)
  * Correct the pg_hba.conf header and rewrite comments, and share one file replace
  * Use the real old pg_hba.conf in the too-long socket path test and restore InstallDir
  * Decide in one place whether a backup error stops the install
  * Test the pg_hba.conf restores on a failed upgrade, and restore only what changed
  * Restore the old pg_hba.conf when an upgrade fails, and show the socket path error
  * Reinstalling the current version's programs keeps its database closes #5120 (#5138)
  * Remove old database folders that hold no database after an upgrade closes #5117 (#5135)
  * Find a database process that has only just started when forcing a stop closes #5116 (#5134)
  * Fix the two lint findings on develop and enforce lint (#5131)
  * Keep non-empty new data when a major upgrade finds a running server closes #5112 (#5121)
  * Upgrade carries over the newest older database, not the first folder closes #5103 (#5114)
  * Wait for the fake postgres command line before scanning in the exited-process test (#5115)
  * Treat pg_hba.conf as Steampipe's only when the checksum line follows the header
  * Check the socket path length before touching the old data directory on upgrade
  * Use each plugin's memory_max_mb even when GOMEMLIMIT is set in the environment closes #5095 (#5096)
  * Rebuild steampipe_plugin_column only when it is missing or wrong closes #5089 (#5090)
  * Say what the pg_hba.conf check does before the backup starts the old postgres
  * Test a downgrade to v2.4.9 and the upgrade after it
  * Never rewrite a pg_hba.conf that Steampipe did not write
  * Stop the test's processes by its install dir alone
  * [dep][actions](deps): Bump goreleaser/goreleaser-action (#5012)
  * [dep][go](deps): Bump github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 from 5.9.2 to 5.10.0 (#5027)
  * Root each local acceptance test file directly under /tmp
